b.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 3\n- Reproducible in Godot 4\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev (de3521ea7) - macOS Unknown (16.0.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M3 Max - Apple M3 Max (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe sensitivity of the panning is painfully slow. The idiom is to usually be able to make the travel relative to the \"real\" distance travelled by the fingers. But here, it's only moving at a fraction of the distance.\n\nAt least, **the travel speed of the camera while rotating should match the travel speed of the camera while panning** (most of the time).\n\nSee the comparison between Godot 3.6, Godot 4.5.dev, Godot 4.5.dev (2D which is OK) and Blender.\n\n| Software | Demo |\n| :---: | :---: |\n| Godot 3.6 (3D) | <video src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fe99e25-d778-43e1-a4d7-255e103b3c96\"> |\n| Godot 4.5.dev (3D) | <video src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75671c15-1c67-4907-af0a-f09f8110603b\"> |\n| Godot 4.5.dev (2D) | <video src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d81355fb-8c73-49fa-ad44-e41c36ee18a3\"> |\n| Blender | <video src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e2604a68-35c3-4707-9f2b-a939ffcdd0b6\"> |\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open Godot\n2. Make sure you're on the 3D editor tab\n3. Pan using the touchpad\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174